Literal block
description: the pipe block scalar — yaml/literal preserves newlines
- >
  The `|` block scalar preserves newlines exactly. Block scalars carry two further modifiers, kept as
  sub-qualifiers of the concrete — they change trailing whitespace and layout, never the meaning of
  the style: **chomping** — clip (the default), strip (`|-`), keep (`|+`) — and the **indentation
  indicator**, an explicit block indent (`|2`) that pins the content indent where the first line
  leaves it ambiguous.
- >
  A block scalar is bounded by its own content indent, so it is self-delimiting — which is what lets a
  tagless block scalar serve as a node's multi-line self-value anywhere among its entries
  ([mixtures](::language:vs-yaml:mixtures)).
